# E1. Contexts compose as requirements, not as ownership
# (ICY-TOWER-CONTEXT-REFACTOR-CENSUS.md, "Context deficiencies", E).
#
# A wrapper context that holds the lower layer's context as a field does not
# install it: wrapper::sprite requires lowlevel::Native transitively, and the
# entry program, which installs only the wrapper, gets MISSING-CONTEXT with
# the chain sprite -> lowlevel::allocate. main-both.bot installs both and
# runs. So an SDL wrapper can turn raw authority into its own context (the
# wrapper mediates raw.bot's direct calls with Platform: no DIRECT error),
# but a layered package (SDL root -> window -> renderer, or SDL -> a game's
# platform context) cannot hide its lower contexts: every layer is installed
# by the entry program, in dependency order, and appears in requirement
# chains. (Only one value of each context type can be installed at all.)
#
# expect interp: MISSING-CONTEXT
# expect compile: MISSING-CONTEXT
# expect cranelift-generic: MISSING-CONTEXT
# expect cranelift: MISSING-CONTEXT
import wrapper

with context wrapper::create()

wrapper::sprite(3)
